diagnostics/list-extrema.em:1:21: `min` needs a List of ordered values, but this is [Bool]
  print([true, false].min())
                      ^^^
Ints, Floats, Strings, and types that adopt `Ordered` have an order. Use another operation for these elements.
diagnostics/list-extrema.em:3:21: `max` cannot choose from [Int?], whose elements may be absent
  print(maybe_numbers.max())
                      ^^^
Use `filter_map` to remove absent values first, so `nothing` can remain the empty-List result.
diagnostics/list-extrema.em:4:11: `min` takes 0 arguments, but this call passes 1
  print([1].min(1))
            ^^^
Match the number of arguments to what the method needs.
